	<td bgcolor="#000000" width="100%" valign="top">
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" > <b>The state of Warriors in PoP - Time for a Change</b></font>
	<p><font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2" >I must admit, I think I'm writing this post calmly and collectively as sort of a desperate attempt to prevent me from fully blowing a gasket and going off on a furious diatribe of profanities.   First an analysis, and then a commentary.<br />
<br />
First, let me give the initial disclaimer so that we dont' go off on tangents.   This analysis deals SPECIFICALLY with the part of the game known as "The Planes of Power", and as such, with the exception of portal stones in PoKnowledge, is limited to the "high level" of the game.   One cannot zone into those planes without being level 46, and realistically, most issues will cover from approximately level 53-65, and will focus the MOST on levels 61-65.    If you have a desire to discuss non-PoP, or general warrior things, then please do so on your own thread.<br />
<br />
The State of Warriors in PoP:<br />
<br />
It can be said that warriors focus on three areas.   Melee damage output, Melee Damage absorption, and The generation and sustenance of an opponent's attention (aggro).   <br />
<br />
Melee Damage Output:<br />
<br />
Planes of Power has been *somewhat* kind to warriors in this regard.   By not having the ridiculous AC on opponents, melee damage seems to be meaningful when compared to the previous expansion.    <br />
<br />
The 50's:  Damage output is fairly good, and many new weapons are available at relatively decent pricing from the Bazaar.   With a minimal investment, warriors seem to be doing just fine in the DPS department.<br />
<br />
There is indeed a drawback to this, and it's the matter called "mudflation".    What mudflation is, is the increasing power of weaponry to "the masses" which obsoletes previous choices and gear.    The reason that "mudflation" has become particularly problematic in the Planes of Power is because the influx of weaponry seems to follow a fascinating trend, which is that there are very few droppable pieces of gear in the early planes which a member of a group hunting there would put on.   All "worthy" gear seems to come from areas which are 2 tiers higher than where people are hunting for experience.   This cheapens the experience of hunting, from one of multiple rewards, in both experience and equippable items, to one of the acquisition of experience points only. <br />
<br />
This problem is significant, one of the most problematic areas in PoP in my view.   Let me say it in a different way.    <br />
<br />
I hunted in Sebilis, and in Howling Stones when I was getting to 60.    There was itemization, and experience.   You had the "double reward".    The thing was, there were items in those zones which you were WILLING to put on.   PoP loot has been *extremely* problematic in this regard.   Generally speaking, items which you have acquired have been found in Tier 3 zones, and by the time you were fighting there, the items that dropped (and quite rarely at that), we in essence auotmatically "bazaar trinkets" to you.   They are almost NEVER equipped by those hunting there.    They make their way to the Bazaar, where people who WOULD make good use of them grab them.   These people are in generally in the mid 50's, and they immediately benefit from those items.   On the other hand, what it THEN does is places a standard on their next upgrade.    They know at this point that in order to even DUPLICATE what they have, they'll have to level throughout the planes into Tier 3 and still won't be rewarded, because they already HAVE the reward from that plane.   It then turns the experience of Everquest into nothing more than advancing the little blue bar and yellow bar of experience.    <br />
<br />
60-65 DPS:   It's good, perhaps the biggest problem being the gap in gear, and lack of upgrades available without raiding.  Two things happen in this level range.  Your level vs. mob level goes up, and you gain 2 damage bonus increases (one at 61 I think and one at 64).   Again, DPS overall is quite acceptable though with the exception of weapon availability.<br />
<br />
A word on the lack of upgrades without raiding:    This is very important to a warrior in particular because it is universally accepted that warriors are the most equipment dependent class in EQ.   Raiding should *always* grant the biggest payoff, but the alternative to raiding shouldn't be *no* payoff, but a smaller one.<br />
<br />
65+AA DPS:   Warriors are *not* hurting at all in this area.   We do substantial damage, and aside from some itemization things and the viability of dual wield (which does need to be looked at and fixed), we do very well, particularly raiding warriors.   Most warriors are quite happy with their damage output.   <br />
<br />
In relation to other classes from a Damage Output perspective:<br />
<br />
Warrior vs. Rogue:   We seem to be ok<br />
<br />
Warrior vs. monk:  Monks are a little weak at the moment in relation to warriors, and should have some sort of DPS output improvement.<br />
<br />
Warrior vs. Ranger:   Seems to be Ok and acceptable<br />
<br />
Warrior Vs. Knight:   Knights are slightly too high in relation to warriors, there needs to be a more clear difference between the two.  Also, the itemization favoritism toward knights is simply wrong to the point of humorous.<br />
<br />
Warrior vs. Beastlord:  Seems reasonable<br />
<br />
Warrior vs. Caster:   Seems reasonable<br />
<br />
Damage Absorption:<br />
<br />
The biggest problem area here is warriors' damage absorption in relation to other classes.   They're not *enough* better to compensate for their clear weakenesses.   This area cannot really be undererstimated.<br />
<br />
The reason that warriors were so far ahead of the other "tanks" in Kunark and early velious was two reasons.   <br />
<br />
1. The cost of Complete heal was higher than the cost of ancillary heals.<br />
<br />
2. Mana was finite and med times were a reality for groups.<br />
<br />
With cleric mana being not an issue with the advent of KEI+ and FT, the argument of tanking efficiency is out the window.  The only reason for tanking efficiency to be a big deal is to conserve a finite amount of mana, but mana isn't really that finite any more.   Because of this, durability differences being not very large pale in comparison to other benefits such as aggro control, ancillary abilities (such as infusing your paty members with mana for even LESS downtime).    <br />
<br />
On the whole, warriors should have a distinctly larger melee damage absorption advantage over others than they currently do.   The point of difference should be noticeable, not a little.<br />
<br />
The Itemization Aspect:<br />
<br />
Warrior only armor pieces offer BARELY greater protection than their Knight Counterparts, while the knight counterparts gain HUGE pluses in terms of manapools, which is the source of their power.   This is... as simply put as I can say... totally unfair to warriors, and needs to be addressed.   If I'm two dimensional, and my competitive counterpart is 3-dimensional, if the sum of my two dimensions is far behind the sum of his three, then he has an unfair advantage over me and this is wrong.   Also, if the ancillary pieces available to my competitor in every slot are identical to those available to me, then the only difference is in the class only armors, where my "advantage" is swallowed up and overshadowed by his "advantages"... there NEEDS to be a greater defensive spread between warriors and all others.<br />
<br />
Taunt:<br />
<br />
Simply put, this is the most screwed up area of EQ.   Warriors are a relic of the past because they cannot reliably and AT WILL get and maintain aggro, while their competitive counterparts CAN with no cost other than a little mana, which in a world of KEI, is again, infinite.<br />
<br />
Notice please, I am not saying that it's broken because warriors and their groups have to work at aggro, but because they do AND their competitive counterparts DONT.   <br />
<br />
Balance it, fix it, it MUST be done, it's screwed up beyond measure.   All other areas of being a warrior are meaningless if the warrior is perceived as not being able to perform this basic task while others are.   Either bring the competitiors down to our level, or bring us up to theirs, I dont' really care.  i suppose I'd prefer the others were brought down, as it wouldn't make the game even more boring.  Whatever it takes FIX IT.    <br />
<br />
The mitigation advantage is VAPORIZED due to the aggro imbalance, because a warrior has to tank unslowed mobs for longer periods of time, and because with the cost of ancillary heals (Sup Remedy, Sup Elixir, and Sup Light) are either the SAME or GREATER mana cost than complete heal, making a warrior a LESS efficient tank, not only from a safety perspective, but also for a mana cost per hour perspective.<br />
<br />
Commentary:<br />
<br />
Nothing has been communicated other than when put on the spot in Fan Faires some vague reference to a "need" to work on long-standing issues comes up to fill the masses with hope only to be unfulfilled, over and over and over again.    <br />
<br />
To me, it's become a matter of character.   If you state the intention to fix something and say that it's broken, and it doesn't happen, then you are a liar, and a deceiver.   There is no other way to put a nice face on it, you have no values, and are not trustworthy.    Sony Online Entertainment is beginning to fit this description.   Certainly they've been guilty at many times of different types of stupidity, mostly in the area of overpromising and underdelivering, but none in such a large way of how they've strung warriors along, stating time and time again that the warrior issues brought to their attention were real and valid issues which needed attention, yet not doing thing one about them.<br />
<br />
Dear SOE, warriors ARE still a class in Everquest, and need to be treated like one.   You communicate on ranger boards, and FOR GODS SAKE you post messages FOR MONKS on the DRUID boards because you won't post on the monk boards due to not wanting to support a Player Auctions funded board.... you DONT post a DAMN thing on warrior boards.. we're the @*(&*(@^&  forgotten stepchild of EQ, we hear vague references from fan faires and keep hope alive.  The hope is fading, I for one have just about stopped believing that you give a rat's ass about warriors' ONGOING issues, when you publicly state something as patently absurd as that you are going to balance melee DPS.... warriors for the most part don't WANT to have DPS screwed with, we want to be viable again, in our ONE job.. tanking.    <br />
<br />
Warrior issues:<br />
<br />
1. BALANCE AGGRO.... FIX IT, IT"S LONG PAST OVERDUE <br />
<br />
2. Make the warrior "defensive advantage" mean something</font></p>
	
