	<td bgcolor="#000000" width="100%" valign="top">
	<font face="verdana,arial,helvetica" size="1" > <b></b></font>
	<p><font face="verdana, arial, helvetica" size="2" >Overall I agree on most of the points.<br />
<br />
Currently i only have issues with aggro in one situation. Exp group that cast on pull or shortly after it. <br />
<br />
normally its ok if its a shammy and me. he malo's then slows. after that slow i taunt and it comes right back to me. <br />
<br />
add druid/enchanter/wiz into the mix and im barly keeping aggro untill my epic procs.<br />
<br />
How about tuning the epic to proc at a higher rate (2hs procs at 2x the rate of the 1hs /boggle)<br />
<br />
with 265 dex i should not have to wait 3 min to proc on some mobs.<br />
<br />
That would do 2 things. give better +hate access to warriors that are not in a guild that are aow ready.<br />
<br />
help us close the gap between us and pally/sk's and warriors.<br />
<br />
Personally I dont think that warriors dont hold taunt well enough. But that pallys and sk's hold it too well. If you have 100% reliable taunt it would be the same as having a +hate procing weapon that proced on each swing... overpowered and trivializing the game<br />
<br />
I could be wrong though</font></p>
	
